[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Report low-level requirements
UID: FMD-LLR-RPT
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Low-level requirements of the report item, written from the code as built: `flightmd_core/models/`,
`flightmd_core/services/` (`score_calculator.py`, `report_builder.py`, `explanation_engine.py`,
`ai_enhancer.py`, `geo_export.py`, `geocoding.py`, `weather_lookup.py`, `airframes.py`),
`flightmd_core/exporters/pdf.py` with its two templates, and `scripts/export_schema.py`. Parents are in
`hlr-rpt.sdoc`. The design is `docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-rpt.md`. Where the code does something surprising
the statement says what the code does; the gaps are listed in section 6 of the design with their problem
report numbers.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Report models (flightmd_core/models/findings.py, metadata.py, __init__.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Severity and Category values
STATEMENT: >>>
`Severity` is a string enum with the values `critical`, `warning`, `info`, `good`. `Category` is a string enum
with the values `oscillation`, `vibration`, `ekf`, `battery`, `gps`, `parameters`, `motors`, `ascent_profile`,
`system`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ParamRecommendation fields
STATEMENT: >>>
`ParamRecommendation` has the required fields `param_name` (str), `current_value` (float), `suggested_value`
(float), `change_direction` (str; the producers write `increase`, `decrease` or `set`, the model does not check
it) and `reason` (str), and the optional `unit` (str, default None).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Finding fields and defaults
STATEMENT: >>>
`Finding` has the required fields `category`, `severity`, `title`, `technical_summary`, `plain_english`,
`recommendation` (str) and `confidence` (float), and the defaulted fields `id` (the first 8 characters of a new
`uuid.uuid4()`), `timestamp_start_ms`, `timestamp_end_ms` (int or None), `t_start_s`, `t_end_s` (float or
None), `chart_data` (dict or None), `param_changes` (list of `ParamRecommendation`, default empty), `kind`
(str or None), `confidence_level` (str or None) and `params` (list of str, default empty).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The schema test fixes the field list and defaults. The random `id` default is not in the schema and is checked
by reading the model.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-031

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Confidence clamp
STATEMENT: >>>
On validation `Finding._fill_derived` sets `confidence` to `min(1.0, max(0.0, confidence))` when it is finite
and to 0.0 when it is NaN or infinite.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Confidence level
STATEMENT: >>>
When `confidence_level` is None, `Finding._fill_derived` sets it from the clamped confidence: `high` at 0.75 or
more, `medium` at 0.4 or more, else `low`. A level given by the producer is kept.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The test checks the `low` case only; the 0.75 and 0.4 thresholds are checked by reading the validator.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Seconds window from the millisecond window
STATEMENT: >>>
`Finding._fill_derived` sets `t_start_s` to `timestamp_start_ms / 1000.0` when `t_start_s` is None and
`timestamp_start_ms` is not, and `t_end_s` from `timestamp_end_ms` in the same way. Values given by the producer
are kept.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Params list includes the changed parameters
STATEMENT: >>>
`Finding._fill_derived` sets `params` to the names already in `params` followed by the `param_name` of each
entry of `param_changes`, with empty names and repeats removed and first-seen order kept. The validator runs
when a `Finding` is constructed or loaded, not when a field is assigned afterwards.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-015

