[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Score (flightmd_core/services/score_calculator.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Weights
STATEMENT: >>>
`ScoreCalculator.__init__` takes an optional dict of module name to weight; when it is None the weights are
`module_weights()` from the analyser registry (modules with weight 0 are absent from it; the built-in weights
sum to 100).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Weighted mean
STATEMENT: >>>
For each result that is assessed and whose weight is above 0, `ScoreCalculator.calculate` sets the result's
`health_score` to `max(0.0, min(100.0, health_score))` and adds `health_score * weight` and `weight` to two
sums. With a total weight above 0 it returns `(overall, label, grade)` where `overall` is the weighted sum
divided by the total weight, held to 0 to 100 and rounded to 1 decimal place, and the label and grade are read
from `BANDS` for that rounded value.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Which results are left out
STATEMENT: >>>
`ScoreCalculator.calculate` sets `assessed` to False on every result with `skipped` true, and leaves out of the
sums every result whose module name has no weight or a weight of 0 or less, and every result with `assessed`
false.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Nothing assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
`ScoreCalculator.calculate` returns `(0.0, "Not assessed", "-")` when the total weight of the results it
counted is 0, which includes an empty result list.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Band table
STATEMENT: >>>
`BANDS` is the list `(90, "Excellent", "A")`, `(80, "Good", "B")`, `(70, "Caution", "C")`,
`(60, "Caution", "D")`, `(50, "Warning", "E")`, `(0, "Critical", "F")`. `ScoreCalculator.get_letter_grade`
and `ScoreCalculator._label` each return the grade or label of the first row whose floor is at or below the
score, and `"F"` or `"Critical"` when no row matches (a negative or NaN score).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Assessed fraction
STATEMENT: >>>
`ScoreCalculator.assessed_fraction` returns the sum of the weights of the results that are assessed and not
skipped, divided by the sum of all weights, rounded to 3 decimal places; it returns 0.0 when the sum of all
weights is 0 or less. A result whose module has no weight adds 0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A NaN module score in the mean
STATEMENT: >>>
In `ScoreCalculator.calculate` a NaN `health_score` of an assessed, weighted module is set to 0.0 before it
enters the mean; positive infinity is held to 100.0 and negative infinity to 0.0, and the result object keeps
the value used.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
COMMENT: >>>
Until problem report PR-002 was fixed, the clamp turned NaN into 100.0, so a broken module score counted as a
perfect one.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-004

