[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Report assembly (flightmd_core/services/report_builder.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Sanitising results
STATEMENT: >>>
`ReportBuilder.build` calls `_sanitise_finding` on every finding of the `findings` argument and on every
finding inside each result; for each result it replaces `key_metrics` by the entries whose value is not None
and is finite (as float), and sets a `health_score` that is not finite to 0.0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Sanitising one finding
STATEMENT: >>>
`ReportBuilder._sanitise_finding` replaces a `chart_data` that is not None by `clean(chart_data)` (numpy
values to Python values, NaN and infinity to None, dict keys to str), removes from `param_changes` every entry
whose `current_value` or `suggested_value` is not finite, and sets `params` to its current names followed by
the names in the remaining `param_changes`, repeats removed, order kept.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the chart data and the params list. No test passes a recommendation with a non-finite value; that
filter is checked by reading the function.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Sanitising metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
`ReportBuilder._sanitise_metadata` dumps the metadata to a dict, applies `clean` to it, sets
`duration_seconds` to 0.0 when it came out None, and validates the dict back into the same model class. A NaN
inside `gps_path` or `gps_path_t_s` becomes None there and the validation raises (those lists take floats
only); the caller prevents this by filling path NaN with 0.0 before the build.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The test covers `duration_seconds`, `max_altitude_m` and `gps_path_hdop`. The failure on a NaN in `gps_path` is
checked by reading the model types and is not exercised.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Order of findings
STATEMENT: >>>
`ReportBuilder.build` sorts the `findings` argument with Python's stable sort on the key
`(SEVERITY_ORDER[severity], -confidence)`, where `SEVERITY_ORDER` is critical 0, warning 1, info 2, good 3 and
an unknown severity counts as 99. The findings inside `analyser_results` are not reordered.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Change sheet: first recommendation wins
STATEMENT: >>>
`ReportBuilder._deduplicate_params` walks the sorted findings and their `param_changes` in order and keeps,
per `param_name`, a copy (`model_copy`) of the first recommendation met. A later recommendation for a kept name
with the same `change_direction` is dropped. The sheet is the kept copies in first-met order. The
recommendations on the findings are not modified.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Change sheet: conflict note
STATEMENT: >>>
For a later recommendation whose `change_direction` differs from the kept one, `_deduplicate_params` records
the note `<direction> to <suggested_value in %g> (<finding title>)`, and after the walk sets the kept entry's
`reason` to `<reason> Another check suggests: <notes joined by "; ">. Review before changing.`
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Report fields set by the builder
STATEMENT: >>>
`ReportBuilder.build` returns a `FlightMDReport` with `report_id` set to `str(uuid.uuid4())`, `overall_score`
from the score tuple (0.0 when not finite), `score_label` and `letter_grade` from the tuple, the summary, file
name and size as given, `metadata` from `_sanitise_metadata`, the sorted findings, the change sheet, the results,
`processing_time_ms` set to the wall-clock milliseconds since `start_time_ms` (0 when `start_time_ms` is None
or 0), `assessed_fraction` from a new default-weight `ScoreCalculator().assessed_fraction(results)`, and
`generated_at` set to the current UTC time formatted `%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-031

