[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Explanations (flightmd_core/services/explanation_engine.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Template table
STATEMENT: >>>
`TEMPLATES` maps a `kind` to a pair (plain-English text, fallback recommendation) for 42 kinds: 3
`oscillation.*`, 5 `vibration.*`, 4 `motors.*`, 7 `gps.*`, 9 `ekf.*`, 4 `battery.*`, 8 `params.*` and 2
`power.*`. The texts are constants; no value from the finding is put into them. The `oscillation.rate_d`
recommendation says to lower the rate D gain, never to raise it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-029
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Plain-English text of one finding
STATEMENT: >>>
`ExplanationEngine._explain` looks `kind` (or the empty string when it is None) up in `TEMPLATES` and sets
`plain_english` to the template text, or to `technical_summary` when there is no template. Any `plain_english`
the producer set is overwritten in both cases.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Recommendation of one finding
STATEMENT: >>>
`ExplanationEngine._explain` leaves `recommendation` as it is unless it is empty or equal to
`technical_summary`; then it sets it to the template recommendation for the `kind`, else to
`CATEGORY_FALLBACK[category]` (texts exist for oscillation, vibration, motors, gps, ekf, battery and
parameters; none for system and ascent_profile), else to `DEFAULT_RECOMMENDATION` ("Consult the log details or
the autopilot's documentation for troubleshooting.").
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: explain_findings and the constructor
STATEMENT: >>>
`ExplanationEngine.explain_findings` is a coroutine that applies `_explain` to each finding in place and
returns the same list; it awaits nothing. The constructor accepts and ignores any arguments and sets
`token_usage` to zero input and output tokens.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-032
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Summary when nothing was assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
When `score_label` equals `"Not assessed"`, `ExplanationEngine.generate_summary` returns one fixed text that
begins "No health score: none of the analysis modules found data they could assess in this log, so this is not
a clean bill of health." and contains no score, no finding and no digit.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-033
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Summary sentences
STATEMENT: >>>
Otherwise `generate_summary` joins with spaces: "Flight health score is `<score, no decimals>`/100
(`<label>`) based on `<duration_seconds, no decimals>`s of log data."; then, if any finding is critical,
"CRITICAL issue(s) detected: `<titles of the critical findings, comma separated>`. Action is required to ensure
flight safety."; else if any is a warning, "Warning(s) detected: `<titles>`. Review the recommendations to
optimize performance and reliability."; else if there are findings, "`<n>` minor note(s); no warnings or
critical issues."; else "No anomalies detected in the checks that could run.". When criticals exist the
warnings are not named.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-034
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Summary names the unassessed modules
STATEMENT: >>>
When `results` is given and any result has `assessed` false, `generate_summary` appends "Not assessed (no
usable data): `<display names, comma separated>`." The same words are used for a module that was skipped
because it raised an error.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-010

