VERIFICATION_NOTE: No test reads these constants or makes a real provider call. A review reads the values.
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-023
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-026

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-036
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Provider selection
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer.__init__` takes `provider`, `anthropic_api_key`, `groq_api_key`, `model` and the old `api_key`. A
non-empty `api_key` with no `anthropic_api_key` is used as the Anthropic key and, when `provider` is None, sets
the provider to `anthropic`. The provider is lower-cased and stripped and defaults to `groq`. For `groq` the
model defaults to `DEFAULT_GROQ_MODEL` and a client is made only when `groq_api_key` is non-empty; for
`anthropic` the model defaults to `DEFAULT_ANTHROPIC_MODEL` and a client is made only when `anthropic_api_key`
is non-empty; any other provider logs a warning and makes no client.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-037
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Client creation
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer._init_groq` imports `openai` and makes `openai.AsyncOpenAI(api_key, base_url=GROQ_BASE_URL,
timeout=REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S, max_retries=MAX_RETRIES)`; `AIEnhancer._init_anthropic` imports `anthropic` and
makes `anthropic.AsyncAnthropic(api_key, timeout=REQUEST_TIMEOUT_S, max_retries=MAX_RETRIES)`. Each sets the
matching call function. On `ImportError` each logs a warning and leaves the client None. No request is sent
when the client is made.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests make both clients with fake keys. The `ImportError` branch and the timeout and retry arguments are
checked by reading the code.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-038
STATUS: Active
TITLE: is_configured and complete
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer.is_configured` is true when a client exists. `AIEnhancer.complete(prompt, max_tokens, system)`
raises `RuntimeError("AI enhancer is not configured")` when it is false; otherwise it awaits the provider call
function with the prompt, `max_tokens` and the system prompt (default `SYSTEM_PROMPT`) and returns its text.
It catches nothing.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-039
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Provider request shape
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer._call_anthropic` calls `messages.create` with the model, `max_tokens`, the system prompt as
`system` and one user message holding the prompt, and returns the joined text blocks, stripped.
`AIEnhancer._call_openai_compatible` calls `chat.completions.create` with the model, `max_tokens` and a system
message followed by a user message, and returns the first choice's content (empty string when None), stripped.
Neither sends any other field.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The tests replace the call function, so neither request is built under test. A review reads the two functions.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-023
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-026

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-040
STATUS: Active
TITLE: clean_text
STATEMENT: >>>
`clean_text(text, limit=300)` converts `text` to str, replaces each control character (U+0000 to U+001F,
U+007F to U+009F) and each zero-width or bidirectional formatting character in its pattern by a space, removes
the characters `<`, `>`, backtick, `{`, `}`, `[` and `]`, collapses all whitespace runs to one space and trims
the ends, and when the result is longer than `limit` cuts it to `limit - 1` characters and appends one
ellipsis character (U+2026).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-041
STATUS: Active
TITLE: numbers_kept
STATEMENT: >>>
`numbers_kept(original, rewritten)` returns True when every match of the pattern `\d+(?:\.\d+)?` in `original`
is also a match of it in `rewritten` (compared as text). It returns True when `original` holds no number, and
it does not look at numbers the rewrite adds.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The test covers a kept and a dropped number. The two last properties are read from the code; they are recorded
as a gap (problem report PR-005).
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-021

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-042
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Summary prompt
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer.polish_summary` builds one prompt: an instruction to rewrite the summary in 2-3 sentences keeping
every fact and number, then between `<report>` and `</report>` the line "Flight duration: `<duration_seconds,
no decimals>`s", the list "Findings:" with one line `- [<SEVERITY>] <clean_text(title, 120)>` for each of the
first 15 findings (or "- None"), and "Current summary:" with `clean_text(base_summary, 1500)`. It calls
`complete(prompt, max_tokens=300)` with the default system prompt. Nothing else from the findings or the
metadata is put in the prompt.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The test checks the tags, the system prompt and that a closing tag in a title is removed. The 15-finding and
length limits are checked by reading the code.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-021
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-043
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Summary fallback
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer.polish_summary` returns `base_summary` unchanged when `is_configured` is false (no call is made),
when `complete` raises any `Exception` (a warning is logged), when the reply is empty, or when
`numbers_kept(base_summary, reply)` is false. Otherwise it returns the reply. It assigns to no attribute of the
findings or the metadata.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the unconfigured case and the dropped-number case. The exception and empty-reply branches are
checked by reading the code.
<<<
