[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-047
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPX document
STATEMENT: >>>
`generate_gpx(report)` builds with ElementTree a `gpx` element (`version="1.1"`, `creator="FlightMD"`,
`xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"`) holding one `trk` with `name` set to `report.file_name` and one
`trkseg`. Per path point it adds a `trkpt` with `lat` = element 0 and `lon` = element 1 formatted `%.7f`, then
`ele` = `_alt(point)` formatted `%.2f` when not None, then `time` = `_iso(t)` when the point has a time. It
returns the XML declaration line followed by the UTF-8 serialisation. An empty or absent path gives an empty
`trkseg`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-048
STATUS: Active
TITLE: KML line
STATEMENT: >>>
`generate_kml(report)` builds a `kml` element (`xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"`) with a `Document`
whose `name` is `report.file_name` and a `Placemark` named "Flight Path" holding a `LineString` with
`altitudeMode` `relativeToGround`, `extrude` 1 and `coordinates` set to the points joined by spaces, each
`lon,lat,alt` with longitude and latitude `%.7f` and altitude `%.2f`, altitude 0 when `_alt` gives None. It
returns the XML declaration line followed by the UTF-8 serialisation. The altitude written is the `gps_path`
value unchanged, whatever its reference.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-017

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-049
STATUS: Active
TITLE: KML path points
STATEMENT: >>>
When the path is not empty and any of `gps_path_hdop`, `gps_path_wind_speed_ms` or `gps_path_t_s` is non-empty,
`generate_kml` adds a `Folder` named "Path points" with `visibility` 0 holding one `Placemark` per path point:
`visibility` 0, a `TimeStamp/when` = `_iso(t)` when the point has a time, an `ExtendedData` with a
`Data name=...`/`value` (formatted `%g`) for each of `t_s`, `hdop` and `wind_speed_ms` that `_at` returns for
the point, and a `Point` with `altitudeMode` `relativeToGround` and `coordinates` `lon,lat,alt` as for the line.
Otherwise no folder is written.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-RPT-017

