[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-RPT-054
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Weather request
STATEMENT: >>>
`fetch_weather` builds the query `latitude` and `longitude` (each `%.4f`), `start_date` and `end_date` both
the flight date, `daily=temperature_2m_max,temperature_2m_min,wind_speed_10m_max,rain_sum` and `timezone=auto`,
and tries `https://archive-api.open-meteo.com/v1/archive` and then `https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast`.
`_get` sends a GET with the header `User-Agent: FlightMD/1.0` and a timeout of 2.0 s and decodes the JSON.
A request that raises any `Exception` is logged and the next host is tried; an answer whose first
`temperature_2m_max` and first `wind_speed_10m_max` are both None also moves on to the next host. When neither
host gives data the "unavailable" dict is returned.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
