`ardupilot_frame(params, vehicle_type)` treats a None vehicle type as `Rover` when `ATC_STR_RAT_P` or
`CRUISE_SPEED` is in the parameters, and `VTOL` as `Plane`. For `Sub` it returns `SUB_CONFIG[FRAME_CONFIG]`.
For `Rover` it returns the `ROVER_CLASS` name of `FRAME_CLASS`, followed by the `ROVER_TYPE` name of
`FRAME_TYPE` when both exist. For `Plane`, or when `Q_ENABLE` is in the parameters, it returns "QuadPlane
`<multirotor name from Q_FRAME_CLASS and Q_FRAME_TYPE>`" (or "QuadPlane" alone) when `Q_ENABLE` is 1 or more,
else "Plane" for a Plane and None otherwise. In every other case it returns the multirotor name from
`FRAME_CLASS` and `FRAME_TYPE`, or None.
